{"operations":[{"content":"The quorum of the general assembly is one third of the members present, as established by the amendment adopted 2 May 2026. [[cite:obs-d0086e18845573f97c098e9c7e8d509c697a2f79 \"Section Quorum is amended: the general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present.\"]]\n\nWhere the amendment of 2 May 2026 and the bylaws differ, the amendment applies. [[cite:obs-d0086e18845573f97c098e9c7e8d509c697a2f79 \"Section Quorum is amended: the general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present.\"]]\n\nThe bylaws state that the general assembly has a quorum when one half of the members are present, but this is superseded by the amendment. [[cite:obs-866f485db2e1ab744efb94a837890dc74426b27a \"The general assembly has a quorum when one half of the members are present.\"]]","expected_sha256":"9d5e7428dfd0bbf65811735e43627aa53c6e5c6ee4b721ba51e586d262924731","kind":"modify","path":"doc/quorum.md"}],"rationale":"Reordered and explicitly cited each statement with exact source spans, preserving all original source citations and clarifying that the amendment supersedes the bylaws."}